id: pm-ill9gv
title: "GH-719: reject or diagnose extension command flags shadowed by pm globals"
description: "Extension command definitions can register flags such as --json whose help text appears extension-owned even though Commander routes the value only to pm global options. Add registration-time validation or an explicit bounded diagnostic, make help truthful, document reserved global names and context.global access, and cover real activation plus invocation instead of API doubles."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-07-26T00:58:26.286Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-26T07:24:45.970Z"
closed_at: "2026-07-26T07:24:43.067Z"
author: "harness:codex"
acceptance_criteria: "Registration rejects or explicitly warns for every extension flag colliding with a canonical or aliased pm global flag; Help and runtime routing cannot imply the value reaches context.options when it is global-only; SDK authoring docs and scaffold guidance expose reserved flags and context.global access; Real installed-extension tests cover activation, help, and invocation at full repository quality gates"
parent: pm-w7mqzt
resolution: "Host-owned global flags are canonical, SDK-visible, activation-enforced, and consumed through context.global by first-party extensions."
expected_result: Extensions cannot shadow host-global flags and first-party author flows remain usable through the host.
actual_result: Reserved spellings fail activation with actionable guidance; all migrated packages consume context.global.author and pass focused/full coverage.
